despite the timeout, but alex wasn't added as a reviewer. I'll add him now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Vkw1vUiBJ4KeYDt4nzz9R2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was rounding half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`) instead of using banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). Its own docstring already said it should use banker's rounding.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`). Now `2.665` rounds to `2.66` (it used to give `2.67`), and `2.675` still rounds to `2.68`, which is what the tests expect.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **Pull request:** The request to open the PR timed out. I checked before trying again and found the PR had been created, but without a reviewer. I added alex separately rather than opening a duplicate.\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the advisory system, so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix follows what the test and the docstring both say. This change gives different results for amounts ending in exactly half a cent when the cent digit is even, so anything downstream that relied on rounding up will see different values. I noted this in the PR. Merging needs a code owner's approval, so I've left the PR for review.", "type": "text"}]}]}